This is the completed bounded compute contribution to the pipeline GPU-wait inventory. It is read-only: no optimization, new profile, GPU run or remote heavy work was performed. It covers54compute entries,36owned source files,323CPU/native-API pattern sites and118owned CUDA synchronization/atomic/loop sites. All inventoried runtime bytes match7de2259b/APP86cb. The read checkout60980adds only the separate row-option tool; its runtime is byte-identical7de.

The selected current region is private batch-prelude Dense: TP8/V100SM70, targetFP16, Q8MTP depth2/confidence0.7, Q8K/V, FP32recurrence,262144nativecontext,24resident sessions and32execution rows. Native family kernels and packed_exact experts are selected. Native router logits and optional padded linears are disabled. GGUF prefill pair planning is unselected. Unique native paged owner attention is selected; the unrelated legacy/native nonowner attention optimization is not.

Historical timing belongs to APP4efe, not current86cb. The protected N24trace has a common10-second window and3071ns clock hull,16target compute calls,4.451s exclusive compute CPU wall,24,026FP32GEMV kernels,140,108total kernels, rank0non-NCCL sum1.861s/NCCL sum6.352s/no-kernel intervals1.787s. Across ranks, similar math1.861–1.914s coexists with varying NCCL3.529–6.663s and gaps1.476–4.557s. These are instrumented wall/kernel sums, not CPU busy cycles, useful utilization or link-saturation proof. Batch86cb changes host preparation and throughput, so old preparation costs are not copied onto it.

The source exposes compute-wide dispatch topology rather than one isolated slow kernel. Each target window loops48layers (36linear/12fullattention), with two HC sequences per layer and a final mixer. TP8output/MoE reductions require96activation collectives, plus48owner-attention collectives, approximately144compute collectives per target forward before head/status traffic. This is a source topology count, not a measured per-window call ledger.

Current FP16decode routing deliberately uses one FP32GEMV per row because native logits are disabled for this private profile. That can produce R*48router GEMVs per target window. Native stable expert selection remains active; it does not remove router launch cost. The historical FP32GEMV count is consistent with this source path but lacks exact parent attribution in the retained aggregate report.

Dense/Concat native helpers retain fixed-M32 ATen products. Small/unprepared/strided cases can still allocate staging and result buffers and copy outputs. Generic native concat holds per-part result tensors unless the special HC-F32/QKV-half direct layout applies. Above32rows, Dense falls into PythonM32tiles with zero/copy/mm/copy; packed experts also fall into selected-weight decode/BMM reference. Current target row32avoids that expert decode cliff, but MTPfc_h uses physicalrows=logicalrows*HCstreams: R96/128can occur even with logical32. Frozen tiler991fand HCWIP43e still create workspace only for logicalBuffer.rows>32, so neither fixes default32MTPphysicalrows; this is a recorded candidate, not implementation during inventory.

FP16GDNcurrently launches one causal native chain per State/linear layer. With localNV6, each launch has six1024-thread CTAs, so its grid can occupy at most six SMs before considering actual occupancy. The batched gdn_multi tree is explicitly excluded forFP16; blindly enabling it would change the recurrence contract. Prefix rejection adds per-layer replay and tail shifts. Native batched State-chain/replay is a credible structural alternative, requiring exact state, conv and accepted-prefix oracles.

PLE can block the CPU feeder inside layer execution: sparse CPU mmap gather, IQ4_NLdecode/FP16conversion, pinned-buffer copy and late H2Dwork. Native PLE conv is still one call per State and launches separate normalization and convolution kernels. Table I/O, PLE layer presence and cached/prefill region determine frequency; no unmeasured page-fault delay is invented.

Compact indexer pooling remains a Torch graph on completed4-row groups after current batch prep: arange/clamp/index_select/where,FP32group sum, FP16storage, normalization padding to preserve CUDA reduction mode, RMS, coordinate RoPE, guard and publication. Reject/cut tails add bounded clone/zeros/index operations. Source scalar metadata controls lengths; these operations do not imply host readback. Native QSA short/mid contexts use dense/selector kernels; above4096pooled groups (~16krawtokens) it falls to Torch scoring/stable sorts and temporary storage. The short prompt trace does not measure that long-context region.

GPUinternal synchronization is separated from CPU-fed waiting. Reachable GDN/family/paged-attention/expert/routing bodies contain CTAbarriers, warp collectives and WMMA synchronization for shared-memory publication/reductions/causal state. They are not presumed removable. AtomicCAS sites are first-error latches, not CAS spin waits. No owned CPU-fed polling loop or threadfence-spin protocol was found in the bounded reachable bodies. NCCL/CUBLAS internals remain opaque; vendor occupancy, memory stalls and internal barriers require later measurements/contracts, not invented source enumeration. Launch error checks/cudaGetLastError are not assumed device-completion fences.

Tensor factories and metadata checks are distinguished from synchronization. empty/zeros, per-part vectors, TensorImpl/view creation and alias/shape validation can consume CPU dispatch time or trigger allocator/lazy-context work. A caching allocator miss may stall, but no per-factory CUDA synchronization is asserted. Explicit status/DMA/pointer-packet/graph retirement boundaries are handed to sibling audits and must be reconciled by Root; this compute inventory does not double-count their historical EventSynchronize cost.

A correctness finding changes qualification provenance: Root actually executed immutable991f/c517 GPUstage session27920,32PASS1.07s/Docker0/normal718FD. Its fixture set allow_fp16_reduced_precision_reduction=False, while7de_family_runtime requiresTrue and allow_fp16_accumulation=False. The result is EXECUTED_WRONG_MATH_REGION, not unrun and not a causal GPU failure. Production APPflags were unchanged. Old raw/stage remain immutable; the same32strict oracles must run with corrected/asserted target flags after inventory before target qualification.

Every entry below has exact source anchor, call chain, condition/frequency, domain/wait mechanism, correctness purpose, evidence scope, candidate and needed proof in compute-inventory.json. Reference/BF16/EXL3/other-codec/optional-plan paths are retained and explicitly not credited as current hot work.

